## Why This Is Asked
This question explores a privacy-preserving on-device machine learning use case with real-world constraints including energy efficiency, latency requirements, data minimization principles, and regulatory compliance. It emphasizes the importance of measurable go/no-go criteria and a concrete break-even timeline for implementation decisions.

## Key Concepts
- On-device machine learning models (autoencoder/isolation forest)
- Energy and performance budgeting for background tasks
- Data minimization and privacy impact assessments
- Go/No-Go criteria and break-even horizon analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
function detectAnomaly(readings, threshold){
  const mean = readings.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)/readings.length;
  const variance = readings.reduce((a,b)=>a+Math.pow(b-mean,2),0)/readings.length;
  return Math.abs(readings[readings.length-1] - mean) > threshold * Math.sqrt(variance);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a cost-benefit framework for cross-app, on-device data sharing with strong privacy constraints and a realistic rollout plan.

## Key Concepts

- On-device cross-app data sharing with strict isolation
- User opt-out and privacy/compliance controls
- Resource budgeting: storage, CPU, energy
- Telemetry delta economics and governance
- Staged rollout and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: anonymize and bucket signals before local merge
function processEvent(event) {
  if (!userOptIn) return;
  const bucket = hash(event.type) % 10;
  buckets[bucket].push(event);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you detect and adapt to schema drift in shared signals?
- What rollback plan and telemetry safeguards would you implement if opt-out is toggled mid-rollout?

## Why This Is Asked

Explore data-locality, privacy, and practical CBA modeling for a lightweight client-side feature in a cloud data platform.

## Key Concepts

- Data locality and offline caching
- Cost modeling: storage, compute, network
- Privacy/compliance: anonymization, retention, audits
- Rollout strategy and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
function estimateCBA(params) {
  // simple cost model placeholder
  const { storagePerUserMB, months, users } = params;
  const storageCostPerMB = 0.02; // hypothetical
  const totalStorage = storagePerUserMB * users * months;
  return totalStorage * storageCostPerMB;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust the model for enterprise vs SMB customers?
- What monitoring would you set to validate the forecast post-launch?

## Why This Is Asked
Assess ability to quantify economics of on-device ML features, balancing privacy, latency, and cloud savings at scale across enterprises.

## Key Concepts
- On-device indexing and embeddings
- Energy budgets and edge compute
- Delta-sync and privacy-compliant telemetry
- Multi-tenant rollout and org-level scaling
- Regulatory/compliance costs and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple relevant cash-flow function for CBA
function cbaNPV(cf, r) {
  let npv = 0;
  for (let t = 0; t < cf.length; t++) {
    npv += cf[t] / Math.pow(1 + r, t + 1);
  }
  return npv;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate the energy model across devices with different hardware?
- How would you quantify productivity uplift from improved search latency in organizations?

## Why This Is Asked
New angle on CBA: gating cross‑app features via an on‑device policy engine, balancing UX, energy, and safety with cloud updates.

## Key Concepts
- On‑device policy engines and gating rules
- Resource awareness (battery, thermal, memory)
- Telemetry footprint and privacy compliance
- Rollout strategy and break‑even analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
function shouldRunFeature(state, policy) {
  if (state.battery < 20) return false;
  if (state.temperature > 45) return false;
  if (state.freeMemory < 200) return false;
  return policy.allowsFeature;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify risk of safety incidents vs false positives?
- What metrics would drive policy update cadence and rollouts across device generations?
